    {
      "url": "https://www.instagram.com/march91magazine/reel/Dd4JuaGsBs5/",
      "thumbnail": "https://instagram.flyp2-1.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t51.82787-15/825320506_18100183832201824_1629111148097149020_n.jpg?stp=dst-jpg_e15_tt6&_nc_cat=111&_nc_map=urlgen_bucketless&ig_cache_key=Mzk5Njk4NzQ0MDgzNTMzNzAxNzE4MTAwMTgzODI2MjAxODI0.3-ccb7-5&ccb=7-5&_nc_sid=58cdad&efg=eyJ2ZW5jb2RlX3RhZyI6IkNMSVBTLnhwaWRzLjU0MC5zZHIudmlkZW9fdXNlcl91cGxvYWRlZF90aHVtYm5haWwuQzMifQ%3D%3D&_nc_ohc=GU8DX8tYjocQ7kNvwE4-99J&_nc_oc=AdoOrIVveZ52S1BKAJy8ysv_xH0a3VHy94J86BKF3I1FkiX636TQV-UpPE883RF6qxrdcsSeDEH8Lc9YGDk6YdXg&_nc_zt=23&_nc_ht=instagram.flyp2-1.fna&_nc_gid=_p8Qhcp4VEZpsVjAbpbdsQ&_nc_ss=7b6a8&oh=00_AQOA8LYk9HWfN4pF_lPWF_cew5xE2x2ISq936SgWND8QBA&oe=6ADFE844",
      "alt_text": "Spending money is inevitable, but what you can control is how and where you spend it. And\nhere budgeting is your best friend, so you don't run bone dry before your father gives you your\nnext pay.\n1) Use the Metro Bus: With its stations going all the way to Saddar and multiple feeder\nbuses, it can save you a lot of money, and give you some fun stories to tell.\n2) Try different street foods: Instead of spending huge amounts of money going to cafés, try\ndifferent street food. Your stomach might disagree sometimes, but your bank account\nwon't.\n3) Thrift: Instead of spending a huge amount of money buying brand-new clothes, try the\nH-9 Bazaar. You'll be surprised by the things you can find there. And if you have doubts,\nremember: washing machines have been invented.\n4) Choose low-cost activities: Go hiking, have a picnic, go window shopping with friends,\nplay board games, or come up with fun activities that aren't so hard on your wallet.\n5) Get cheap friends: If your current friends are hard on your wallet, throw them out and get\ncheapskates as friends. This will save you the money you spend trying to fit in.\n6) Carry cash for daily spending: Take out only what you plan to spend that day. It's much\nharder to accidentally spend Rs. 2,000 when you physically only have Rs. 500 in your\npocket.\n7) Make a “fun money” limit: Don't completely ban yourself from spending. Give yourself a\nfixed amount for cafés, snacks, shopping, etc.\n8) Keep an emergency fund: Even if it's a small amount, keep some money aside for\nunexpected expenses. Because somehow, the moment you're broke, everything\ndecides to go wrong at once.\n9) Honestly, kbhi kbhi ghar aur hostel se bhi kha liya kro khana. Har roz bahar se khana\nzaroori nahi hai. Ghar ka khana is literally right there. Hostel ka khana… Well, character development hai.\nShare your budgeting hacks with us in the comment section!"
    },
